1600 BM$="Man: I am Archbishop Mellis. You sorcerers know me as the King of the\North.":GOSUB 5100
1610 BM$="King of the North: When I learned that David had inherited the blood of the\Devil King, I had to get rid of him. Under normal circumstances I would have\spared your life, Susanna...":GOSUB 5100
1620 BM$="King of the North: However, I know that you are pregnant with his child.\Thus, you must share his fate.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1630 BM$="Susanna: So you really were the King of the North... How did you know we'd\be coming?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1640 BM$="Connors: According to Lord Mellis, those men who helped you were\detectives under our service. One of them was someone Lord Mellis knew\very well. In fact, I remember him as well.":GOSUB 5100
1650 BM$="Connors: It stands to reason that he'd tell you about us, so I called the\church to prepare for your arrival. Opening the door to this room would\activate the curse.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1660 BM$="King of the North: Susanna. With your death, the blood of the Devil King will\be severed, ushering in a peaceful world. This was never a battle between\justice and evil. It was only ever a battle for revenge.":GOSUB 5100
1670 BM$="King of the North: I must kill you, that much is unavoidable. With that said, I\am a servant of God. I shall pray for your souls, so that you and David may\spend eternity together in Heaven.":GOSUB 5100
1680 BM$="King of the North: Connors, there is no need to cast a killer curse upon her.\Send her to God using your dagger.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1690 COMMON FO:BM$="Connors: I would have liked to witness your great power in action my Lord,\but I shall do as you say.":GOSUB 5100
1695 GOSUB 9020:'
1700 BM$="Connors took out his dagger and approached Susanna.":GOSUB 5100
1710 BM$="Connors: I want you to know this is nothing personal. I must follow his\orders. Please don't hold it against me.":GOSUB 5100
1720 GOSUB 6150:BM$="The moment Connors raised his dagger, Susanna quickly pulled out the\dagger from the table, launching herself at her executioner.":GOSUB 5100
1730 BM$="The two daggers hit their marks at the same time. Both Connors and\Susanna's hearts had been pierced.":GOSUB 5100
1740 GOSUB 6160:BM$="They collapsed next to David, their blood pouring onto the floor.":GOSUB 5100
1750 BM$="King of the North: No, Connors!! Urgh... My act of kindness cost him his life...!\...Mgh?! David! You're still alive?!":GOSUB 5100
1760 GOSUB 6170:BM$="David, who had been thought to be dead, stood up, blood still pouring from\his chest.":GOSUB 5100
2000 BM$="David: You have underestimated the strength of my blood. Though faintly,\David's heart is in fact still beating. My power was able to keep it alive,\even under the influence of your sorcerous effigy!":GOSUB 5100
2010 BM$="David: King of the North. Through your naivety, I have witnessed the blood\of Connors - a northern tribesman. As long as David's heart is beating, he\shall awaken as the Devil King, and cast eternal curses upon you!":GOSUB 5100
2020 GOSUB 9050:GOSUB 9575:BM$="Still bleeding, David began to cast a spell aimed at the King of the North.":GOSUB 5100
2030 GOSUB 6180:BM$="King of the North: AAARGH!!":GOSUB 5100
2040 GOSUB 9540:GOSUB 6190:BM$="Blood began to gush out of the King of the North's face.":GOSUB 5100
2045 GOSUB 9515:GOSUB 6200:BM$="At the sight of the bloodied face of their king, the northern sorcerers\fled from the room in a panic.":GOSUB 5100
2050 GOSUB 9555:GOSUB 6210:BM$="Blood kept gushing out of the King of the North's body. His robes were\stained in the crimson liquid, and soon he was lying in a pool of his own\blood.":GOSUB 5100
2070 COMMON FO:GOSUB 6220:GOSUB 9030:BM$="But once the King of the North had breathed his last, David also collapsed.":GOSUB 5100:'
